# The level 1 tests that must pass (not skip) in the testbed jobs of ci.yml and in the kernel matrix of nightly.yml:
# each job loads this file into its environment (`grep -E '^[A-Z0-9_]+=' .github/level1-tests.env >> "$GITHUB_ENV"`) and
# names the lists with `-expect-pass`, so a renamed or vanished test, or one that skips on a kernel, fails the job
# instead of leaving it green. NAME=comma-separated test names, one line per list; the acceptance maps in
# docs/development.md say what each list covers.

# The level 1 tests of port forwarding (M35a): both testbed jobs name them with -expect-pass, so a renamed or
# vanished test fails the job instead of leaving it green (the acceptance map in docs/development.md).
M35A_LEVEL1=TestAForwardReachesTheListenersOfADeviceOnTheRealKernel,TestAForwardDoesNotCountIPv6ConnectionsToItsEntryInterfaceOnTheRealKernel,TestRulesOnTheTargetDecideForwardedConnectionsOnTheRealKernel,TestACutWindowResetsAnEstablishedForwardedConnectionOnTheRealKernel,TestAForwardFollowsANewEntryAddressAndANewDeviceAddressOnTheRealKernel,TestAForwardPassesDockersForwardPolicyThroughDockerUser,TestForwardsReachTheDeviceFromBothSidesAndFollowItsAddress,TestAForwardFollowsANewUplinkAddress,TestADeviceFaultDoesNotImpairAForwardedConnection,TestARuleOnTheDeviceCutsAnEstablishedForwardedConnection,TestAForwardCountsTheConnectionsAnAllowRuleAcceptsOnTheRealKernel,TestAnAllowAllRuleDoesNotOpenTheManagementNetworkWhileAManagementForwardWorks,TestAManagementForwardAnswersAPeerBehindARouterOfTheManagementNetwork,TestWithoutTheUplinkDefaultAnAllowAllRuleStillDoesNotOpenTheManagementNetwork,TestAMatrixEntryOpensTheManagementNetworkBehindAManagementInterfaceOfItsOwn,TestAMatrixEntryOpensTheManagementNetworkThroughTheUplink,TestAForwardReachesAnIdleDeviceWhoseNeighborEntryIsStale,TestTheRepliesOfAManagementForwardedConnectionStayOffTheUplinkAfterTheForwardIsDeleted,TestTheGuardKeepsADeviceOutOfAManagementRoleWireGuardNetworkUntilAMatrixEntryOpensIt

# The level 1 tests of scenario runs (M15): the steps of a run on the real kernel and the real clock, within 100 ms of
# their schedule where the machine is accurate, an abort and an expired lease that take the run's overlays out.
M15_LEVEL1=TestAScenarioRunsOnTheRealKernelAndItsStepsAreOnTime,TestAnAbortOnTheRealKernelTakesTheOverlaysOfTheRunOut,TestAnExpiredLeaseOnTheRealKernelRemovesTheFault

# The level 1 tests of checks and zero-hit warnings (M16): a scripted device that comes back after a cut or gives up, a
# device that resolves a name or talks to an allowed and a disallowed server, the limit of the traffic checks under a drop, and a
# fault that matches nothing, on the real kernel.
M16_LEVEL1=TestChecksPassForADeviceThatReconnectsOnTheRealKernel,TestChecksFailForADeviceThatDoesNotReconnectOnTheRealKernel,TestAFaultThatNeverMatchesIsAZeroHitWarningOnTheRealKernel,TestTrafficNotSeenWithExceptDecidesOnTheRealKernel,TestDNSQuerySeenDecidesForADeviceOnTheRealKernel,TestTheTrafficChecksDoNotSeeWhatTheGatewayDropsOnTheRealKernel

# The level 1 tests of packet captures (M17): the AF_PACKET sockets of the executor on the loopback interface, the
# executor protocol over its socket (these need CAP_NET_RAW, so they carry the build tag testbed and run in the
# testbed jobs only), and the captures over the API on the real kernel against a capture on the device itself.
M17_LEVEL1=TestACaptureOnTheLoopbackHoldsExactlyTheSelectedTraffic,TestTheSnapLengthCutsPacketsAndKeepsTheOriginalLength,TestACaptureOfThePcapFormatIsReadableAndHasTheLinkType,TestTheSizeLimitEndsTheCaptureAndTheFileStaysWithinIt,TestTheDurationEndsTheCapture,TestACaptureStopsWhenTheDiskIsAlmostFullAndRefusesToStartOnOne,TestARingBufferCaptureKeepsTheNewestPackets,TestAMissingInterfaceAndABadFilterAreRefusedAtTheStart,TestACanceledContextEndsTheCaptureWithAnError,TestAFullDiskIsTheDiskLowReason,TestStopIsIdempotentAndTheFirstReasonStays,TestADeviceCaptureHoldsTheFramesOfItsAddressInBothDirectionsAndNoOthers,TestASelectorCaptureHoldsOnlyTheMatchingTrafficOfTheDevice,TestAFilterTooLargeForTheKernelIsAppliedInUserSpace,TestACaptureStartsStreamsItsCountersAndEndsWhenItIsStopped,TestAStopForTheEndOfARunIsPassedOn,TestOnlyMaxCapturesRunAtOnceAndASlotComesBackWithTheEnd,TestACaptureOnAFullDiskIsRefusedAndStopsWhenTheDiskFills,TestTheFilesOfACaptureBelongToTheOwnerOfItsDirectory,TestACaptureOverTheSocketHasTheSameEventsAndEndsWithAStop,TestAConnectionThatBreaksEndsItsCaptureAndGivesTheSlotBack,TestTheSocketNamesTheReasonsACaptureIsRefused,TestTheSocketRefusesACaptureWithTheErrorAndKeepsServing,TestARedialingClientOpensCapturesToo,TestACaptureOfADeviceIsExactlyTheCaptureOnTheDeviceItselfOnTheRealKernel,TestASelectorCaptureHoldsTheConnectionsItNamesOnTheRealKernel,TestTheUplinkCaptureShowsThePacketsAfterNATOnTheRealKernel,TestAWireGuardNetworkIsCapturedAsRawIPOnTheRealKernel,TestARunWithCaptureTrueAttachesTheTrafficOfItsTargetOnTheRealKernel,TestALowDiskStopsTheCaptureButNotTheRunOnTheRealKernel,TestTheExecutorRefusesACaptureOnAVolumeBelowItsLimitOnTheRealKernel

# The level 1 tests of chaosctl (M18): `with` under a delay on the wire and its cleanup after a failing command, runs from a
# file with the exit codes 0 and 1 against a scripted device, an abort on a signal, `wait device`, and a fault whose
# lease is not renewed, on the real kernel.
M18_LEVEL1=TestChaosctlWithDelaysThePathAndCleansUpAfterAFailingCommandOnTheRealKernel,TestChaosctlRunPassesForADeviceThatReconnectsOnTheRealKernel,TestChaosctlRunFailsForADeviceThatDoesNotReconnectOnTheRealKernel,TestChaosctlAbortsARunOnASignalAndTakesTheFaultOutOnTheRealKernel,TestChaosctlWaitsForADeviceAndItsConnectionOnTheRealKernel,TestAFaultWhoseLeaseIsNotRenewedLeavesTheRealKernelOnItsOwn

# The level 1 tests of Kea's packet socket after a link flap of a test port (#64), named the same way: the testbed
# test and the tests against the real Kea, which run as root only.
I64_LEVEL1=TestDHCPAnswersAgainAfterTheTestPortFlappedDuringAnApply,TestTheHostReadingCountsACarrierFlapOnARealKernel,TestReopenConfiguresKeaAgainWithAnUnchangedConfiguration,TestKeaRetriesASocketItCouldNotOpen

# The older tests against the real Kea (internal/kea/kea_testbed_test.go, startKea; I64-05): they run as root
# only, so they carry the build tag testbed and are named the same way, and a run in which one skips fails. The
# tests against the real Kea without the tag (TestKeaAcceptsTheRenderedConfiguration, and the engine's restart
# test, which runs as root only) are in packages with tagged tests, so the testbed runner builds and runs them too.
KEA_LEVEL1=TestTheClientDrivesARealKea,TestLeasesArePagedPastTheLimit,TestKeaAcceptsTheRenderedConfiguration,TestTheConfigurationIsSentAgainToAKeaThatRestarted
